  "tldr": "The paper targets the exact all-procedure minimax risk for the full global treatment effect on a revealed uniform simple random regular network under the endpoint empirical second-moment class of Kandiros--Harshaw--S\\'{a}vje. The proposed answer is \\(d_n^2/[n\\log(d_n+1)]\\). A balanced two-arm Bayes argument supplies the converse, while a log-tuned neighborhood-seed design and Rao--Blackwell estimator supply the upper construction. The new proof angle avoids an unbounded Boolean inclusion--exclusion expansion: a sparse-range switching argument controls radius-two collisions, and an exact fourth-trace decomposition reduces the remaining dense range to one signed four-distinct-vertex reachability moment. The central open question is to prove that cancellation-sensitive moment uniformly for \\(n^{2/5}\\le d_n=o(\\sqrt n)\\).",
