  "related_work": "KandirosHarshawSavje2026Minimax, Introduction, Proposition 2.2, Corollary 5.4, Appendix E.4, and the Conclusion, supplies the exact decision-theoretic framing and the published \\(d_n/n\\)-to-\\(d_n^2/n\\) bracket; the matched theorem strictly tightens that corollary on the same class. KandirosEtAl2024ConflictGraph, Algorithm 1 and Theorem 4.1, supplies conflict resolution, exact desired-exposure probabilities, and the covariance-operator proof pattern, but its generic GATE certificate remains of order \\(d_n^2/n\\). UganderYin2023RGCR, Section 3 and Theorem 4.8, randomizes graph decompositions and integrates exposure probabilities, but its guarantee is procedure-specific and assumes bounded outcomes and restricted growth. CookGoldsteinJohnson2018, Theorem 1.1, controls the nontrivial adjacency spectrum directly under the uniform simple regular law through \\(d=O(n^{2/3})\\); it does not control Boolean radius-two collisions. Xu2025SwitchingGraphMatrices, Theorems 2.10--2.11 and the trace-moment construction, treats fixed polynomial graph matrices under regular-graph dependence, whereas \\(B_G\\) is a thresholded reachability matrix whose leading diagrams must cancel jointly. AbbeBoixRalliSandon2020, Corollary 1 and Section 2.2, separates Boolean graph powering from walk counts, but its sparse Erd\\H{o}s--R\\'{e}nyi and small-radius conditions exclude the present dense regular range. CooperEtAl2002RandomRegular determines ordinary one-colour independence asymptotics, not balanced opposite-arm radius-two packing. HarshawSavjeWang2022Riesz characterizes linear design-based estimators but does not establish a complete class for the jointly optimized nonlinear minimax game. Public January 2026 Li--Li slides disclose a lower bound for Horvitz--Thompson risk and a one-arm upper construction under stronger all-assignment outcome bounds; the slides explicitly list the full two-arm estimator as ongoing and are non-archival, so they are disclosed but not us